        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T21:46:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This causes test case \"test_lock_flash_control_register\" to fail, because in addition to unlocking option bytes, this call has the side effect of unlocking control register for bank 0.\n\nWe want the flash_physical test to test just one behavior at a time, so instead of calling unlock_optb() here, this function should only do:\n\n\t\tSTM32_FLASH_OPTKEYR(0) \u003d FLASH_OPTKEYR_KEY1;\n\t\tSTM32_FLASH_OPTKEYR(0) \u003d FLASH_OPTKEYR_KEY2;\n\nand unlock_optb() should call unlock_flash_option_bytes().",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 177,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "ce4d6646138554e1809babab369f317b62775604",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e20cfd1_ff711bfe",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/flash-stm32h7.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T21:46:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Similar to unlock_flash_option_bytes, this should be the other way around: lock_flash_option_bytes() should just do \n\n\tSTM32_FLASH_OPTCR(0) |\u003d FLASH_OPTCR_OPTLOCK;\n\nAnd commit_optb() should call lock_flash_option_bytes(). This is because commit_optb() has the extra effect of locking flash control registers, and we want to be able to test just the option bytes behavior.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "ce4d6646138554e1809babab369f317b62775604",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
